The attached image, corresponding to Figure 10 in the PDF, illustrates Nano-11's ability to induce local inflammation and facilitate antigen uptake by immune cells in skeletal muscle 24 hours post-injection. The top row shows muscle tissue injected with Nano-11+OVA, revealing numerous recruited Mac-2+ monocytes/macrophages, MHCII+ antigen-presenting cells, and 1A8+ neutrophils, many containing intracellular Nano-11 (red). In contrast, the bottom row, showing tissue injected with soluble OVA alone, displays a scarcity of inflammatory cells. This indicates that Nano-11 significantly enhances the recruitment and activation of immune cells and promotes the uptake of adsorbed antigens, crucial for its adjuvant effect.